/-!
# Faithful cyclotomic and seed Galois characters exist

Theorem statement: `HorizontalPadicL.seedCyclotomicGaloisCharacters_exist_v4`
(`5081d5cd-7574-4b9a-91ed-315ac2eb2b14`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25.

Proof: submission `c6074e07-d461-42d1-97d8-59b1053d5598`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

For a positive level N, a prime p, a positive exponent m, and a primitive seed Dirichlet character
eta satisfying the stated order and coprimality conditions, there is a common finite Galois
realization of the actual cyclotomic character modulo p^m N and the seed character, with a seed
value of full character order.

## Explanation of the source proof

Take a cyclotomic field containing roots of unity of orders sufficient for both the modulus $p^mN$
and the conductor of the seed character. Its finite Galois group carries the usual cyclotomic
character modulo $p^mN$. Composing the cyclotomic action at the seed conductor with the primitive
seed Dirichlet character gives the seed Galois character.

The standard cyclotomic description of the Galois group proves both action laws and identifies the
kernel fixed fields. A generator of the finite image of the seed character provides the
distinguished element having full order. These data assemble into
`SeedCyclotomicGaloisCharacterDataV2`.

<!-- Generated by add_prove2me_provenance.py -->
-/

